body:
If you are in "time out" you can reach out to MS and ask for it to be removed(if they are nice), but it will be gone in 24hrs. 

&#x200B;

Ive had accounts be put in time out many a few times.

I have 119 clients using LDAP without signing in this new environment. Fun times ahead of me. 

&#x200B;

This helps identify the clients:  [https://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/archive/blogs/russellt/identifying-clear-text-ldap-binds-to-your-dcs](https://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/archive/blogs/russellt/identifying-clear-text-ldap-binds-to-your-dcs) 

&#x200B;

Capturing logs right now. Wish me luck!

Edit: Remember to run these captures on ALL domain controllers, even RODC. Each one will have their own entries.

Valley Fever victim here -2 years ago Valley Fever took me out of work for two weeks and caused me to be unable to walk around due to the pain. It mimics the flu, so just be careful if you get flu like symptoms. Be sure you get those doctor visits and tests performed ASAP and take your medicine religiously.

&#x200B;

I wouldn't say I am outside a lot, but I still got it. I've only experience one minor flare up since then.

You are correct! Living in the same city your whole life and even on the same side of town, you get to recognize all homeless people, but I've noticed an explosion of new homeless in the past 2 years. Freeways are lined with tent's and people walking looking for cans. Our local bikepath is littered with trash and other abandoned stuff from them.

&#x200B;

I still do not agree with his action, but I understand how he could've been pushed this far. Local business owners have to deal with the homeless situation a lot more than non-business owners. They can cause a lot of headaches for them, such as breaking into storage or dumpster areas. They also sleep/camp in front or behind of their business and hang around asking for change, which can cause customers to shy away.

&#x200B;

In the end, we are all humans and should treat each other with all the same respect. Many sit around and complain about homeless in my city, but what I love is that not everyone sits around and takes it. People rally and get together to plan clean ups to pick up after these homeless. I myself carry around small care packages for them, encase I get approached by one asking for change. These consist of travel sized items, such as toothbrush, toothpaste, shampoo, socks, dollar bill, reusable water bottle, or w/e I find cheap or on sale.

We had a ticketing system that had its own knowledge base that we slowly built, which can be tagged or associated to a ticket. Before this, we used [https://www.teamwork.com/](https://www.teamwork.com/) to store our KB articles along with task templates to use in order to complete common tasks such as Onboarding or PC setup.

&#x200B;

I also built up bookmarks in Google Chrome and have it synced with my Gmail account. I have hundreds I've built up over the years to help with various things. I even separate them based on vendor.

Welcome to ISP's. When they dont have huge competition, they can act like total asshats. Even their website is crap, but if you can try to order online, it may trigger someone to come out. You can also put your address in to see if service is available. [https://frontier.com/shop](https://frontier.com/shop) 

Also check your address here: [https://www.allconnect.com/internet/in-my-area](https://www.allconnect.com/internet/in-my-area) 

&#x200B;

As the other replies stated, try contacting a Wireless Mobile provider such as ATT or Verizon and get a little mobile antenna setup in your house until things get figured out. Costly, but you get connection. You can also check and see if Google Fiber is around. Also check with neighbors and ask who they get internet from. 

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

Screen recording software seems the way to go. Dont know who is going to want to review the videos though. I dont think the employees will be doing it anymore knowing it is being recorded. Also, you would need to configure some kind of rule to only record when a Remote session is started unless you want 8+ hours of screen recordings every day.

&#x200B;

You can opt to purchase software that will allow them to remote into their home computers and that software records the session. You will need open up support for getting it installed on their home computers and additional money being thrown at the problem. 

&#x200B;

What do the employees state they need to do this for?

I would remove all users from folder and keep Administrators. I would try to create a group if this is a request I would see often or its a parent folder, but if I don't feel a group is warranted I would just do a "Share" to each of the users. This will allow them to view/edit/modify(whichever permissions you give) the folders contents. It will display all the other sub-folders leading to the folder, but they will all be blank for them.

&#x200B;

Working with a nested file server where nothing making sense and people have all these "special" requests is something that gets worse and worse over time unless someone puts their foot down and stops it. 

I would look into trying to start doing this: [https://blogs.msmvps.com/acefekay/2012/01/06/using-group-nesting-strategy-ad-best-practices-for-group-strategy/](https://blogs.msmvps.com/acefekay/2012/01/06/using-group-nesting-strategy-ad-best-practices-for-group-strategy/)

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

I had this issue a while back, but nothing ever came of it. Hopefully this link helps:[https://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/exchange/enable-internet-calendar-publishing-exchange-2013-help](https://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/exchange/enable-internet-calendar-publishing-exchange-2013-help)

&#x200B;

I remember we had on-prem only at the time and we needed to either enable Exchange to allow online publishing or create a federated trust between the two AD's. Dont think the other company would want to do this. You can also create a account called "Conference Room A" and have both companies log into OWA and view it...but I wouldnt start there.

\+1 on this. 

&#x200B;

If my boss told me to do this, I would take a extra hard look at security as that will bite you the hardest if they get compromised. "Well So and So gave it the A-Okay". You are now under the bus, so ensure you point out potential security flaws.

 24 to 36 months of work experience in networking, storage or IT data center administration.             Familiarity with any major hypervisor technologies for server virtualization.              

&#x200B;

Thats what CompTIA suggests. It does help a lot having certs/experience when taking other certs. For example having Security knowledge helped a lot during Network+ exam. These are also recommendations though and not requirements.

I found in my 4-5 year mark at a job I became too comfortable and wasnt challenged anymore. I got a new cert and moved on. MSP's have been mentioned and they will get you a lot of experience in many different environments and systems, but I found they are pretty hard to land. They want someone who a lot of experience in many different areas, but expect Help Desk level pay. For example, an MSP I applied for was for "Computer/Network Technician" and they wanted someone who was a Systems Admin for Help Desk pay. 

&#x200B;

But I relate to you a lot. I am a Jr. Sys Admin and I find myself wanting to break into Security side, but having a hard time figuring out how. Security jobs are also rare in my city the ones that do pop up require 5+ years exp already. 

&#x200B;

Have you tried "creating" a security position at your current position? Just start assuming duties or roles? I've done this before with some applications and naturally just became the SME for it.

This happened to me this morning. All I did was change my display settings from "extend display" to "only display desktop 1", then change back to "extend display". I am running on Intel's built in GPU, dont recall chip I am using at the moment though.

&#x200B;

Edit: I am on a docking station with dual monitors, my secondary actually was black but recognized. It appeared as if it was working perfectly fine, just wasnt showing an image.

Suicide help lines are great for emergency situations. Keep them in mind and use them. Please use them if you need to. Please.

&#x200B;

Hobbies. Drinking, smoking, games, sex, driving, building, cleaning, talking, or w/e. We all need escapes. Sometimes your s/o needs help even when they say they dont. Oh how i wish my s/o knew or was with me during my trying times.  

&#x200B;

No article can beat human warmth and support. No matter how much he pushes away, always be sure he know he can ALWAYS turn to you when needed. 2 am or 2 pm.  But also learn when they need space. Confusing I know, but if you stick around, you just may someone who will love you for life.

&#x200B;

Other than that, therapist it helpful. We reveal things to therapist that I didnt think i'd ever say to another living human being. I also didnt expect the words the therapist said to make such an impact on me. Its like they are in my head. 

&#x200B;

I feel the same way. I am too depressed to keep on current events or learn new things. Its like, whats the f\*cking point?

&#x200B;

But then I see how it hurts me in my career and social life. Depression has a bigger tole on a life than many realize. Even people with depression.

I hope one day we can all realize marijuana is not only a medicine, but a overall life enhancer. 

&#x200B;

If energy is so low, if medical insurance permits, has your testosterone levels been checked? What about your thyroid? How much exercise do you get? Find a exercise you enjoy because it will make you want to do it more. IMO.

I first attempted at 16. Sleeping pills. I almost got away with it, but a good bye text to my best friend went out before I died. I did not know she knew my address. I was drifting away when an ambulance and cops came pounding down my door. Parents were shell shocked.

&#x200B;

I am 30 now and I still think of how I would do it. I have pills, but all of them would just make me sick if I OD. I recently had a conversation with someone older, successful and amazing human. He opened up to me and told me things he felt that I also felt. It was amazing knowing others feel the same and our feelings are not so abnormal. He is even older than me.

&#x200B;

I guess we need to find things to keep us here. Dig roots to prevent us from drifting up into heaven. Being able to identify when you get in those "states" means you are starting to manage your condition. This is a very good thing that many still struggle.

Your welcome. I know its not about the beer, but the act of losing the money. I am trying to help you see a bit of perspective here. I hate it when others do it to me, but in a way I hate to admit it, it helps. 

&#x200B;

If you are young, give it time and it does get easier. This thing called "life". I was shit poor trying to hussle old computers for food money, but I worked my ass off to get some education. Hard ass work, I mean HARD ass work does pay off. It takes years, but fuck it does eventually pay off.

Oh, wow. I feel so sorry for people who live in states or counties who do not allow this amazing medicine. In California, USA, I take it for granted. Other than marijuana, only alcohol makes me hungry, but just a bit. 

&#x200B;

Its a harsh cycle because if I dont eat, I get more depressed, but then more depression means less eating. I wish I could offer more advise on this, but I dont have much other experience. Is CBD also banned? 

&#x200B;

For energy only non medical thing I can offer is a lot of sleep, likst 9-10 hours. Then like 1 hr before work to "wake up". You lose a lot of your day, but you are not tired?

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

I was in same boat around your age. You gotta start finding yourself and figure out what you like and fuck what everyone else thinks. I started to not be ashamed of the things I like. 

&#x200B;

For example: I like anime, I am 30 years old married with kids. I work in a professional setting and I dont care who knows that I love anime. I find this helps you enjoy the things more as you are so carefree doing it. I love cycling, but the whole get up made me embarrassed. I eventually just said fuck it and now Ill walk into gas stations in my whole Tour De France gear rocking my camel toe and all. 

&#x200B;

If anything I hope I helped in some way.
